1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,989
The elevator in his building had twelve buttons.

2
00:00:04,239 --> 00:00:05,923
Tonight, it had thirteen.

3
00:00:06,173 --> 00:00:08,301
There was no thirteenth floor.

4
00:00:08,551 --> 00:00:10,750
So, of course... he pressed it.

5
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,766
The doors opened onto a dark, silent hallway.

6
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:19,421
And standing there, waiting for him... was himself.

7
00:00:19,671 --> 00:00:22,984
Same glasses. Same smile. Just... older.

8
00:00:23,234 --> 00:00:27,165
The man stepped forward and opened his mouth to say something...

9
00:00:27,215 --> 00:00:28,924
and the doors closed.

10
00:00:33,474 --> 00:00:35,634
The next night, the button was back.

11
00:00:37,784 --> 00:00:41,412
So was the man. But now, he looked ten years older.

12
00:00:41,662 --> 00:00:45,622
The doors always stayed open for exactly five seconds.

13
00:00:48,262 --> 00:00:52,647
And every visit, the man on floor thirteen was ten years older.

14
00:00:52,997 --> 00:00:57,081
Downstairs, one day went by. Up there... a whole decade.

15
00:00:58,431 --> 00:01:02,712
So every night, he went back. He had to know what the man wanted.

16
00:01:04,162 --> 00:01:08,313
On day three, the old man shouted. No sound came out.

17
00:01:10,563 --> 00:01:15,730
On day five, he held up a note. The doors closed before he could read it.

18
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:21,527
On day eight, he jammed his cane between the doors.

19
00:01:22,477 --> 00:01:24,223
It snapped like a pencil.

20
00:01:26,473 --> 00:01:30,615
On day eleven, he could barely stand. His hair was white.

21
00:01:30,865 --> 00:01:32,290
And he was crying.

22
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:37,803
On day thirteen, he pressed the button one last time.

23
00:01:39,453 --> 00:01:41,260
The hallway was empty.

24
00:01:41,410 --> 00:01:45,105
No old man. Just a piece of paper on the floor.

25
00:01:45,355 --> 00:01:47,071
He stepped out to grab it.

26
00:01:48,055 --> 00:01:50,293
Behind him, the doors closed.

27
00:01:50,443 --> 00:01:53,345
And the elevator went down. Without him.

28
00:01:54,895 --> 00:01:58,547
He unfolded the paper. It was his own handwriting.

29
00:01:58,797 --> 00:02:00,439
Don't press thirteen.

30
00:02:02,189 --> 00:02:05,804
Then he looked at his hands. They were already getting older.

31
00:02:06,354 --> 00:02:09,852
Far below, the elevator started coming back up.

32
00:02:10,402 --> 00:02:15,518
The doors opened. And inside, pressing thirteen for the very first time...

33
00:02:15,668 --> 00:02:17,747
was him. Young. Confused.

34
00:02:18,097 --> 00:02:22,224
Now he knew why the old man never finished his sentence.

35
00:02:22,474 --> 00:02:27,150
He opened his mouth to warn him... and the doors began to close.

36
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:31,308
He has twelve more visits. Twelve more chances.

37
00:02:31,658 --> 00:02:34,545
And this time... he's going to write it bigger.
